//! Portable 128-bit native vectors and canonical lane masks.
//!
//! The six shapes have size and alignment 16. Arithmetic lowers to dedicated
//! AMIR vector operations; instruction count depends on the target and backend.
//! Integer arithmetic wraps at lane width. Float comparisons follow IEEE NaN
//! rules: only `ne` is true for an unordered pair; signed zero compares equal.
//! Slice loads/stores check the complete range before accessing any lane, need
//! only scalar alignment, and do not promise a single machine memory operation.
//!
//! ## Platform
//! `native` · `wasm32` · `bare-metal`
module std.core.simd

import std.core.intrinsics as intrinsics
import std.core.slice as slice

/// Native 128-bit vector of 4 `f32` lanes. Construct through its methods.
public struct F32x4 {}

/// Native 128-bit vector of 2 `f64` lanes. Construct through its methods.
public struct F64x2 {}

/// Native 128-bit vector of 4 `i32` lanes. Construct through its methods.
public struct I32x4 {}

/// Native 128-bit vector of 8 `i16` lanes. Construct through its methods.
public struct I16x8 {}

/// Native 128-bit vector of 16 `u8` lanes. Construct through its methods.
public struct U8x16 {}

/// Native 128-bit vector of 2 `i64` lanes. Construct through its methods.
public struct I64x2 {}

// Compiler ABI declarations are validated by identity and exact signature.
